---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { assets } from "../../data/releases";
---

<Docs title="Installation" description="Install the RUDRA toolchain on Linux, macOS or Windows." slug="installation">
  <p class="lead">The RUDRA toolchain ships as downloadable release assets. The current 1.1.0 build targets Linux x86_64; macOS and Windows installers are available from the 1.0.1 release.</p>

  <h2>Available builds</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>Asset</th><th>Release</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {assets.map((a) => (
        <tr><td>{a.platform} ({a.arch})</td><td><code>{a.file}</code></td><td>{a.release}</td></tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Linux (x86_64)</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="sh" code={`tar -xzf rudra-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
cd rudra-linux-x86_64 && ./install.sh
rudra version`} />
  <p>The installer copies <code>rudra</code>, <code>rudrac</code>, <code>ruxpkg</code> and <code>rudra-lsp</code> into <code>~/.local/bin</code> by default. Ensure that directory is on your PATH.</p>

  <h2>macOS (Apple Silicon)</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="sh" code={`sudo installer -pkg rudra-macos-arm64.pkg -target /
rudra version`} />

  <h2>Windows (x86_64)</h2>
  <p>Run the <code>.exe</code> installer, then open a new terminal and run <code>rudra version</code>.</p>

  <h2>Verify your download</h2>
  <p>Always confirm the SHA256 checksum shown on the <a href="/downloads">Downloads</a> page before installing:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="sh" code={`sha256sum rudra-linux-x86_64.tar.gz`} />

  <div class="callout callout-warn">
    <h4>About the binaries</h4>
    <p>The distributed toolchain binaries are dynamically linked executables. See <a href="/transparency">Transparency</a> for details.</p>
  </div>
</Docs>
